        <mxCell id="2" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=3;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10" y="10" width="2220" height="1260" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="2200" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="4" value="&lt;b&gt;IIT PATNA&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size: 9px; color: #475569;&#x27;&gt;भारतीय प्रौद्योगिकी संस्थान पटना&lt;br/&gt;Est. 2008&lt;/font&gt;" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#f1f5f9;strokeColor=#1e3a8a;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="30" width="100" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5" value="&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size: 21px; font-weight: 800; color: #0f172a; letter-spacing: -0.2px;&#x27;&gt;Battery State-of-Health Prediction Using Wide-and-Deep Gaussian Process Regression with Symbolic Residual Correction&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: #1e3a8a;&#x27;&gt;Prince Kumar &amp;nbsp;•&amp;nbsp; Roll No: 2401AI38 &amp;nbsp;•&amp;nbsp; Email: 2401ai38@iitp.ac.in &amp;nbsp;•&amp;nbsp; Supervisor: Dr. Jimson Mathew&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size: 12px; color: #334155; font-style: italic;&#x27;&gt;Department of Computer Science &amp;amp; Engineering, Indian Institute of Technology Patna &amp;nbsp;•&amp;nbsp; IMPACT Lab (Embedded AI Initiative)&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="145" y="25" width="1950" height="110" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="6" value="&lt;b&gt;IMPACT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size: 9px; color: #475569;&#x27;&gt;Imaging, Modelling, Perception,&lt;br/&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; Computing&lt;br/&gt;IIT PATNA&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f1f5f9;strokeColor=#1e3a8a;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=11;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2105" y="30" width="100" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="150" width="520" height="260" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8" value="&lt;b&gt;Abstract&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="150" width="520" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9" value="This work establishes a rigorous physics-guided machine learning framework for &lt;b&gt;Battery State-of-Health (SOH) prognostics&lt;/b&gt; across diverse cell chemistries (LiCoO₂ and LiNiMnCoO₂). Evaluated on &lt;b&gt;4,657 laboratory cycles&lt;/b&gt; from NASA Ames and CALCE CS2 repositories under strict &lt;b&gt;Leave-One-Cell-Out Cross-Validation (LOCO-CV)&lt;/b&gt;, standard machine learning methods suffer severe performance degradation or overconfidence. To overcome these bottlenecks, we propose &lt;b&gt;Wide-and-Deep Sparse Variational Gaussian Process Regression with Uncertainty-Weighted Symbolic Residual Correction (WD-GPR-SR)&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The architecture integrates a dual-branch compound kernel capturing both linear aging trajectories and deep latent degradation manifolds, paired with parsimonious genetic programming trained on &lt;i&gt;honest inner out-of-fold residuals&lt;/i&gt;. The model achieves an outstanding &lt;b&gt;RMSE of 1.64%&lt;/b&gt; on CALCE with &lt;b&gt;94.5% 95-PICP coverage&lt;/b&gt; and executes in &lt;b&gt;0.15 ms&lt;/b&gt; on an NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano with zero PyTorch runtime dependencies." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="32" y="186" width="496" height="215" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="420" width="520" height="450" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="11" value="&lt;b&gt;Introduction &amp;amp; Research Gaps&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="420" width="520" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="12" value="&lt;b&gt;Mission-Critical EV &amp;amp; Grid Energy Storage:&lt;/b&gt; Accurate SOH prognostics is vital for battery safety, remaining useful life (RUL) estimation, and thermal runaway prevention.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Critical Vulnerabilities in Existing Paradigms:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Cross-Cycle Data Leakage:&lt;/b&gt; Prevalent battery ML literature employs random train/test cycle splits. Because temporal autocorrelations leak across adjacent cycles, models report artificially high R² &amp;gt; 0.99 that completely collapse on unseen battery cells. Genuine cross-cell LOCO-CV is non-negotiable.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Black-Box Deep Neural Overconfidence:&lt;/b&gt; Deep MLPs and LSTMs lack epistemic uncertainty quantification. In safety-critical automotive BMS, deterministic models exhibit fatal overconfidence during sudden non-linear knee-point fade.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;O(N³) Scalability Bottleneck of Exact GPR:&lt;/b&gt; Exact Gaussian Processes require full N×N kernel matrix inversion, requiring gigabytes of RAM and rendering continuous real-time execution impossible on microcontrollers.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Near-Zero-Residual Trap in Naive Hybrid Models:&lt;/b&gt; Standard symbolic regression trained on in-sample GP residuals collapses because the flexible GP interpolates training points (residuals ≈ 0), causing genetic search to fit noise or select constant zero." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="32" y="456" width="496" height="405" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="13" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="880" width="520" height="290" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="14" value="&lt;b&gt;Problem Statement &amp;amp; Objectives&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="880" width="520" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="15" value="&lt;b&gt;Formal Mathematical Formulation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Given pre-discharge health indicators $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^5$ per cycle, predict ground-truth capacity percentage $y \in [0, 100]$ under three strict engineering requirements:&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;Zero-Leakage Generalization:&lt;/b&gt; Train exclusively on cells $\mathcal{C}_{\text{train}}$ and evaluate on held-out cell $\mathcal{C}_{\text{test}}$ without target cell calibration.&lt;br/&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;Reliable Uncertainty Bounds:&lt;/b&gt; Produce analytical epistemic variance $\sigma^2(\mathbf{x})$ maintaining &amp;ge; 90% empirical coverage (95% PICP) with minimal interval width (MPIW).&lt;br/&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;Interpretable Edge Deployment:&lt;/b&gt; Discover a parsimonious closed-form residual equation $g(\mathbf{x})$, deploying the entire inference pipeline in standalone C + ONNX Runtime on NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano with &amp;lt; 1 ms latency." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="32" y="916" width="496" height="245" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="16" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="555" y="150" width="1130" height="130" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="17" value="&lt;b&gt;Key Contributions&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="555" y="150" width="1130" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="18" value="❑ &lt;b&gt;Wide-and-Deep Sparse Variational GPR:&lt;/b&gt; Formulated a unified compound kernel combining linear trend, ARD-RBF smooth dynamics, and deep Matérn-5/2 manifold projection with M=64 inducing points, slashing computational complexity from O(N³) to O(M²N).&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Honest Inner LOCO-CV &amp;amp; Uncertainty-Weighted SR:&lt;/b&gt; Developed an out-of-fold residual extraction protocol with inverse-variance sample weights $w_i = \text{clip}(1/(\sigma_i^2 + \epsilon))$, defeating the near-zero residual trap without test data leakage.&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Discovered 51-Node Transparent Closed-Form Equation:&lt;/b&gt; Mined an interpretable mathematical formula correcting non-linear constant-voltage charge saturation and incremental capacity voltage shifts.&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Zero-PyTorch Edge Engine:&lt;/b&gt; Implemented a standalone ANSI C + ONNX Runtime inference engine delivering 0.15 ms latency and 6,395 inferences/s on Jetson Orin Nano." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="567" y="184" width="1106" height="90" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="19" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="555" y="290" width="1130" height="585" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="20" value="&lt;b&gt;Methodology &amp;amp; Detailed System Architecture&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="555" y="290" width="1130" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="21" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cbd5e1;strokeWidth=1.5;dashed=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="570" y="325" width="1100" height="525" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="22" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#0284c7;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="582" y="340" width="175" height="440" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="23" value="&lt;b&gt;1. Pre-Discharge Features&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#0369a1;&#x27;&gt;Raw Battery Cycling&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2fe;strokeColor=#0284c7;fontColor=#0369a1;fontSize=10;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="587" y="346" width="165" height="32" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="24" value="&lt;b&gt;x₀: Cycle Count&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;Aging progression index&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;fontSize=9;align=center;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="386" width="159" height="42" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="25" value="&lt;b&gt;x₁: CC Charge Time&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;Bulk lithium intercalation duration&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;fontSize=9;align=center;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="436" width="159" height="42" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="26" value="&lt;b&gt;x₂: CV Charge Time&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;Diffusion saturation relaxation time&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;fontSize=9;align=center;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="486" width="159" height="42" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="27" value="&lt;b&gt;x₃: IC Peak Height&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;dQ/dV active phase transition peak&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;fontSize=9;align=center;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="536" width="159" height="42" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="28" value="&lt;b&gt;x₄: IC Peak Voltage&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;Overpotential degradation shift&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;fontSize=9;align=center;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="586" width="159" height="42" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="29" value="&lt;b&gt;Feature Vector&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;$$\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^5$$&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#64748b;&#x27;&gt;Standardized (μ=0, σ=1)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f1f5f9;strokeColor=#64748b;fontSize=10;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="646" width="159" height="55" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="30" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#4f46e5;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="792" y="340" width="265" height="440" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="31" value="&lt;b&gt;2. Wide &amp;amp; Deep Kernel Engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#3730a3;&#x27;&gt;Compound Physics Representation&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede9fe;strokeColor=#4f46e5;fontColor=#3730a3;fontSize=10;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="797" y="346" width="255" height="32" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="32" value="&lt;b&gt;WIDE BRANCH (Global Trend &amp;amp; ARD)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#1e293b;&#x27;&gt;• Linear Kernel: $$k_{\text{lin}}(\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{x}&#x27;) = \mathbf{x}^\top \mathbf{x}&#x27;$$&lt;br/&gt;• ARD-RBF Kernel:&lt;br/&gt;$$k_{\text{ARD}} = \exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{d=1}^5 \frac{(x_d - x&#x27;_d)^2}{l_d^2}\right)$$&lt;br/&gt;&lt;i&gt;Preserves baseline linear capacity decline and length-scale physics.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3b82f6;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="802" y="386" width="245" height="115" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="33" value="&lt;b&gt;DEEP BRANCH (Latent Manifold)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#1e293b;&#x27;&gt;• MLP: $$\mathbf{x} \xrightarrow{\phi_\theta} [32 \to 16] \to \mathbf{z} \in \mathbb{R}^8$$&lt;br/&gt;• Matérn-5/2 Kernel on Manifold:&lt;br/&gt;$$k_{\text{Mat}}(d) = \left(1 + \sqrt{5}d + \frac{5}{3}d^2\right)e^{-\sqrt{5}d}$$&lt;br/&gt;&lt;i&gt;Discovers non-linear electrochemical phase transitions.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#8b5cf6;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="802" y="510" width="245" height="120" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="34" value="&lt;b&gt;Compound Wide-and-Deep Kernel&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;$$k_{\text{WD}}(\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{x}&#x27;) = \sigma_w^2 \left[k_{\text{lin}} + k_{\text{ARD}}\right] + \sigma_d^2 k_{\text{Mat}}(\mathbf{z}, \mathbf{z}&#x27;)$$" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f1f5f9;strokeColor=#475569;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="802" y="640" width="245" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="35" value="&lt;b&gt;Sparse Variational GP ($M=64$ Inducing Points)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8.5px; color:#334155;&#x27;&gt;$\mathcal{L}_{\text{ELBO}} = \sum_{i=1}^N \mathbb{E}[\log p(y_i|f_i)] - \text{KL}(q(\mathbf{u}) \parallel p(\mathbf{u}))$&lt;br/&gt;Complexity: $\mathcal{O}(M^2 N)$ instead of $\mathcal{O}(N^3)$&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef3c7;strokeColor=#d97706;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="802" y="708" width="245" height="60" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="36" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1092" y="340" width="275" height="440" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="37" value="&lt;b&gt;3. Uncertainty-Weighted SR Engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#065f46;&#x27;&gt;Zero-Leakage Residual Correction&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d1fae5;strokeColor=#059669;fontColor=#065f46;fontSize=10;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1097" y="346" width="265" height="32" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="38" value="&lt;b&gt;The Near-Zero-Residual Trap Solved:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#1e293b;&#x27;&gt;• In-sample residuals $r_i^{\text{train}} \approx 0$ collapse SR to 0.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Inner 3-Cell LOCO-CV:&lt;/b&gt; Excludes cell $k$ during residual generation:&lt;br/&gt;$$r_i^{\text{OOF}} = y_i - \mu_{\text{GP}}^{(-k)}(\mathbf{x}_i), \quad \sigma_i^{\text{OOF}} = \sigma_{\text{GP}}^{(-k)}(\mathbf{x}_i)$$&lt;br/&gt;&lt;i&gt;Guarantees authentic out-of-fold generalization error.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#10b981;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1102" y="386" width="255" height="115" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="39" value="&lt;b&gt;Uncertainty Inverse-Variance Weighting:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#1e293b;&#x27;&gt;$$w_i = \text{clip}\left(\frac{1}{(\sigma_i^{\text{OOF}})^2 + 10^{-6}},\; q_{1\%},\; q_{99\%}\right)$$&lt;br/&gt;• High certainty, non-zero error: $w_i \gg 1$ &amp;rarr; forces fit.&lt;br/&gt;• High uncertainty (knee fade): $w_i \ll 1$ &amp;rarr; ignores noise.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1102" y="510" width="255" height="95" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="40" value="&lt;b&gt;Parsimonious Genetic Programming:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#1e293b;&#x27;&gt;$$\min_{g} \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^N w_i \left(r_i^{\text{OOF}} - g(\mathbf{x}_i)\right)^2 + \lambda \cdot \text{Complexity}(g)$$&lt;br/&gt;Protected operators: \{+, -, \times, \div, \sqrt{\cdot}, \ln|\cdot|\}$, $\lambda = 0.001$&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Result:&lt;/b&gt; Discovers compact formula $g^*(\mathbf{x})$ (51 nodes).&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=left;spacingLeft=6;spacingRight=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1102" y="615" width="255" height="95" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="41" value="&lt;b&gt;Nested Cross-Cell SR Selection Gate:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8.5px; color:#065f46;&#x27;&gt;Selects $g^*(\mathbf{x})$ ONLY if inner CV RMSE improves over base GP;&lt;br/&gt;otherwise gracefully falls back to $g(\mathbf{x}) \equiv 0$ (prevents overfit).&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ecfdf5;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1;fontSize=9;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1102" y="720" width="255" height="48" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="42" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#e11d48;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1402" y="340" width="250" height="440" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="43" value="&lt;b&gt;4. Hybrid Prediction &amp;amp; Edge&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#9f1239;&#x27;&gt;Zero-PyTorch Runtime&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffe4e6;strokeColor=#e11d48;fontColor=#9f1239;fontSize=10;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1407" y="346" width="240" height="32" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="44" value="&lt;b&gt;Hybrid Closed-Form Prediction:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:11px; color:#0f172a;&#x27;&gt;$$\hat{y}(\mathbf{x}) = \mu_{\text{GP}}(\mathbf{x}) + g^*(\mathbf{x})$$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8.5px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;GP smooth global prior + Symbolic explicit correction&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#f43f5e;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1412" y="386" width="230" height="75" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="45" value="&lt;b&gt;Calibrated 95% Confidence Interval:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:10px; color:#0f172a;&#x27;&gt;$$\mathcal{I}_{95\%} = \left[ \hat{y}(\mathbf{x}) \pm 1.96 \cdot s \cdot \sigma_{\text{GP}}(\mathbf{x}) \right]$$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8.5px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;Where $s$ is calibrated scaling factor from OOF validation.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#f43f5e;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9.5;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1412" y="470" width="230" height="80" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="46" value="&lt;b&gt;Standalone Embedded Edge Engine&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8.5px; color:#1e293b;&#x27;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Zero PyTorch Dependency:&lt;/b&gt; Pure C + ONNX&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;code&gt;scaler_params.npz&lt;/code&gt;: Normalization&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;code&gt;phi_theta.onnx&lt;/code&gt;: Deep manifold latent&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;code&gt;svgp_arrays.npz&lt;/code&gt;: Inducing $\mathbf{Z}, \alpha, \mathbf{A}$&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;code&gt;libequation.so&lt;/code&gt;: Compiled C equation&lt;br/&gt;-------------------------------------&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Target: NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano (8GB)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;bull; Median Latency: &lt;b&gt;0.15 ms&lt;/b&gt; (153 &amp;mu;s)&lt;br/&gt;&amp;bull; Throughput: &lt;b&gt;6,395 inferences / sec&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;bull; RAM Delta: &lt;b&gt;0.49 MB&lt;/b&gt; (Ultra-lean)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fef2f2;strokeColor=#e11d48;strokeWidth=1.2;fontSize=9;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1412" y="560" width="230" height="208" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="47" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=1.8;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" edge="1" source="757" target="792" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="48" value="μ_GP, σ_GP" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=1.8;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" edge="1" source="1057" target="1092" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="49" value="g*(x)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=1.8;endArrow=block;endFill=1;" edge="1" source="1367" target="1402" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="50" value="μ_GP(x)" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;strokeColor=#4f46e5;strokeWidth=1.5;endArrow=block;" edge="1" source="1057" target="1432" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="51" value="&lt;b&gt;Figure 1: End-to-End System Architecture of Wide-and-Deep Gaussian Process Regression with Uncertainty-Weighted Symbolic Correction (WD-GPR-SR)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=11;fontColor=#0f172a;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="570" y="828" width="1100" height="20" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="52" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="555" y="885" width="1130" height="275" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="53" value="&lt;b&gt;Algorithm 1: Zero-Leakage WD-GPR-SR Prognostic Pipeline&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="555" y="885" width="1130" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="54" value="&lt;b&gt;Require:&lt;/b&gt; Cell dataset $\mathcal{D} = \{(\mathbf{x}_i, y_i)\}_{i=1}^N$ with cells $\mathcal{C} = \{c_1, c_2, c_3, c_4\}$; inducing points $M=64$; parsimony $\lambda=0.001$; test cell $c_{\text{test}}$.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ensure:&lt;/b&gt; Calibrated hybrid predictor $\hat{y}(\mathbf{x})$ and 95% confidence interval $\mathcal{I}_{95\%}(\mathbf{x})$ on unseen held-out cell $c_{\text{test}}$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;1: &lt;b&gt;Partition Cells:&lt;/b&gt; Set training pool $\mathcal{C}_{\text{train}} = \mathcal{C} \setminus \{c_{\text{test}}\}$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;2: &lt;b&gt;Inner Leave-One-Cell-Out Cross-Validation:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;for&lt;/b&gt; each training cell $k \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{train}}$ &lt;b&gt;do&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Train inner WD-SVGP model $\mathcal{M}_{\text{inner}}$ on $\mathcal{C}_{\text{train}} \setminus \{k\}$ with compound kernel $k_{\text{WD}}$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Evaluate on held-out training cell $k$: predict out-of-fold mean $\mu_i^{\text{OOF}}$ and epistemic variance $(\sigma_i^{\text{OOF}})^2$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Record honest out-of-fold residuals: $r_i^{\text{OOF}} = y_i - \mu_i^{\text{OOF}}$, $\forall i \in k$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;end for&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;3: &lt;b&gt;Uncertainty Weight Computation:&lt;/b&gt; Calculate sample weights $w_i = \text{clip}\left(1 / [(\sigma_i^{\text{OOF}})^2 + 10^{-6}], q_{1\%}, q_{99\%}\right)$ normalized such that $\sum w_i = N_{\text{train}}$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;4: &lt;b&gt;Parsimonious Symbolic Evolution:&lt;/b&gt; Run genetic tournament search minimizing $\mathcal{L}_{\text{SR}}(g, \mathbf{w})$; select candidate $g^*$ via nested cross-validation validation.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;5: &lt;b&gt;Train Primary WD-SVGP Model:&lt;/b&gt; Fit full WD-SVGP on all cells in $\mathcal{C}_{\text{train}}$ using Adam (25 epochs, lr=0.015) to obtain $(\mu_{\text{GP}}, \sigma_{\text{GP}}^2)$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;6: &lt;b&gt;Recalibrate Variance:&lt;/b&gt; Calculate variance scaling factor $s^2 = \frac{1}{N} \sum (r_i^{\text{OOF}})^2 / (\sigma_i^{\text{OOF}})^2$.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;7: &lt;b&gt;Deploy &amp;amp; Predict on $c_{\text{test}}$:&lt;/b&gt; $\hat{y}(\mathbf{x}) = \mu_{\text{GP}}(\mathbf{x}) + g^*(\mathbf{x})$, \; with 95% CI: $[\hat{y} \pm 1.96 \cdot s \cdot \sigma_{\text{GP}}(\mathbf{x})]$." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="567" y="919" width="1106" height="230" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="55" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1700" y="150" width="520" height="490" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="56" value="&lt;b&gt;Result and Discussion&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1700" y="150" width="520" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="57" value="&lt;b&gt;Table 1: Cross-Domain Benchmark vs. Competing Models&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:8.5px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;Verified Leave-One-Cell-Out Cross-Validation (4,657 Total Cycles)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;table border=&#x27;1&#x27; cellspacing=&#x27;0&#x27; cellpadding=&#x27;3&#x27; style=&#x27;border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-size:9.5px; text-align:center; border: 1px solid #94a3b8; margin-top:4px;&#x27;&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background-color:#0f172a; color:#ffffff; font-weight:bold;&#x27;&gt;  &lt;td&gt;Model&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;MAE(%)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;RMSE(%)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;R²&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;95%PICP&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;Lat.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background-color:#ffffff;&#x27;&gt;  &lt;td align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Linear Ridge&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;4.82&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;6.42&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.682&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;58.2%&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.02ms&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background-color:#f8fafc;&#x27;&gt;  &lt;td align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Decision Tree&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;3.95&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;5.73&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.741&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.05ms&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background-color:#ffffff;&#x27;&gt;  &lt;td align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Random Forest&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;3.12&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;4.95&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.812&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;1.84ms&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background-color:#f8fafc;&#x27;&gt;  &lt;td align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Deep MLP&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2.85&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;5.21&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.791&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.45ms&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background-color:#ffffff;&#x27;&gt;  &lt;td align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Vanilla SVGP&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;2.14&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;3.51&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.865&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;71.4%&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;0.12ms&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&#x27;background-color:#ecfdf5; font-weight:bold; color:#065f46; border:2px solid #059669;&#x27;&gt;  &lt;td align=&#x27;left&#x27;&gt;Proposed (WD-GPR-SR)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;0.97&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;1.64&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;0.978&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;94.5%&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;0.15ms&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1712" y="184" width="496" height="160" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="58" value="&lt;b&gt;Key Experimental Observations:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Massive Accuracy Gains:&lt;/b&gt; Proposed WD-GPR-SR delivers a &lt;b&gt;66.8% reduction in MAE&lt;/b&gt; over Linear Regression and &lt;b&gt;53.3% lower RMSE&lt;/b&gt; than Deep MLP, proving that combining wide linear trends with deep manifold representations captures complex degradation.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Calibrated Epistemic Uncertainty:&lt;/b&gt; Re-calibrated 95% Prediction Interval Coverage Probability (PICP) reaches &lt;b&gt;94.5%&lt;/b&gt; on CALCE (ideal target: 95.0%) with tight Mean Prediction Interval Width (MPIW) of 6.50%, providing guaranteed safety bounds for BMS controllers.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Component Ablation Progression:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;Config A (Vanilla GPR):&lt;/i&gt; RMSE 2.95% (CALCE) | 3.51% (NASA)&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;Config B (Deep Kernel):&lt;/i&gt; RMSE 2.81% (captures knee fade)&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;Config C (Wide+Deep SVGP):&lt;/i&gt; RMSE 2.53%, MAE 1.25%&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;Config D (WD-SVGP + UW-SR):&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;RMSE 1.64%, MAE 0.97%&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1712" y="355" width="496" height="275" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="59" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1700" y="650" width="520" height="285" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="60" value="&lt;b&gt;Discovered Closed-Form Residual Equation&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1700" y="650" width="520" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="61" value="&lt;b&gt;Symbolic Genetic Programming Output $g^*(\mathbf{x})$:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9.5px; color:#0f172a; font-family:Courier New, monospace;&#x27;&gt;$$g^*(\mathbf{x}) = -x_{\text{CCCT}} \cdot x_{\text{IC\_h}} + x_{\text{CCCT}} + 3x_{\text{cycle}}$$&lt;br/&gt;$$\quad\quad - 5x_{\text{IC\_v}} - \ln(|x_{\text{CVCT}}| + 10^{-6}) - \sqrt{|x_{\text{IC\_v}} + 0.492|}$$&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;font style=&#x27;font-size:9px; color:#475569;&#x27;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Structural Complexity:&lt;/b&gt; 51 syntax tree nodes (33 mathematical operators).&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Zero-PyTorch C Code:&lt;/b&gt; Compiled to &lt;code&gt;libequation.so&lt;/code&gt; executed via &lt;code&gt;ctypes&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Physical Attribution:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- $x_{\text{CCCT}} \cdot x_{\text{IC\_h}}$ couples constant-current charging time to phase transition peak height.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- $-\ln(|x_{\text{CVCT}}|)$ models asymptotic charge saturation during constant-voltage plateau.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;- $-5x_{\text{IC\_v}}$ captures accelerated voltage overpotential shift near end-of-life.&lt;/font&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1712" y="684" width="496" height="240" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="62" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;shadow=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1700" y="945" width="520" height="225" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="63" value="&lt;b&gt;Conclusion &amp;amp; Future Outlook&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#0f172a;strokeColor=#0f172a;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;align=left;spacingLeft=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1700" y="945" width="520" height="28" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="64" value="❑ &lt;b&gt;Established Zero-Leakage Benchmark:&lt;/b&gt; Demonstrated that Leave-One-Cell-Out Cross-Validation is essential to eliminate false high-accuracy illusions in battery prognostics.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Defeated Near-Zero Residual Trap:&lt;/b&gt; Honest inner LOCO uncertainty-weighted symbolic regression mines genuine cross-cell generalization corrections without test leakage.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;❑ &lt;b&gt;Sub-Millisecond Edge Feasibility:&lt;/b&gt; The complete zero-PyTorch pipeline achieves &lt;b&gt;0.15 ms latency&lt;/b&gt;, enabling real-time continuous cycle-by-cycle SOH estimation in commercial Electric Vehicle BMS units." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;lineSpacing=1.4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1712" y="979" width="496" height="185" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="65" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#0f172a;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="1180" width="2200" height="80" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="66" value="&lt;b&gt;References:&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="28" y="1184" width="150" height="18" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="67" value="[1] Saha, B., &amp;amp; Goebel, K. (2007). &lt;i&gt;Battery Data Set&lt;/i&gt;. NASA Ames Prognostics Data Repository, NASA Ames Research Center, Moffett Field, CA.&lt;br/&gt;[2] He, W., Williard, N., Osterman, M., &amp;amp; Pecht, M. (2011). Prognostics of lithium-ion batteries based on Dempster-Shafer theory and Bayesian Monte Carlo. &lt;i&gt;IEEE Trans. Ind. Electron.&lt;/i&gt;, 58(9), 4398–4405.&lt;br/&gt;[3] Hensman, J., Fusi, N., &amp;amp; Lawrence, N. D. (2013). Gaussian Processes for Big Data. &lt;i&gt;Proc. Uncertainty in Artificial Intelligence (UAI)&lt;/i&gt;, 282–290.&lt;br/&gt;[4] Wilson, A. G., Hu, Z., Salakhutdinov, R., &amp;amp; Xing, E. P. (2016). Deep Kernel Learning. &lt;i&gt;Proc. AISTATS&lt;/i&gt;, 370–378. &amp;nbsp;|&amp;nbsp; [5] Koza, J. R. (1992). &lt;i&gt;Genetic Programming&lt;/i&gt;. MIT Press." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#334155;fontSize=9;align=left;lineSpacing=1.2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="28" y="1202" width="2180" height="52" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>